--
-- Long division:
--   Problem:      What governs fluid momentum?
--   Known answer: ρ(∂v/∂t + v·∇v) = -∇p + μ∇²v
--   PNBA mapping:
--     ρ   = IM  (Identity Mass = fluid inertia)
--     v   = N   (Narrative = velocity flow)
--     -∇p = -B·P (Behavior × Pattern = pressure gradient)
--     μ∇²v = B-axis viscous resistance
